## Why This Is Asked
Assesses cost-aware design of privacy-preserving observability with edge processing, cross-region deployment, and go/no-go decisions.

## Key Concepts
- Edge compute budgeting
- Privacy-first telemetry
- Data retention and regional regulations
- Multi-region cost models
- Rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function cba(params) {
  // simple cost model
  const deviceCost = params.deviceCPU * 0.1 + params.deviceMem * 0.05;
  const deltaCost = (params.deltaKB / 1024) * 0.02;
  const centralCost = params.retentionMonths * 1000 * 0.01;
  return deviceCost + deltaCost + centralCost;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for GDPR/CCPA across regions?
- What metrics would tie cost to business value beyond raw savings?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to translate a complex edge-ML rollout into a precise 2-year CBA, balancing hardware, cloud costs, and real-world benefits like downtime and maintenance savings.

## Key Concepts

- Edge computing and on-device training
- Federated learning and privacy implications
- CAPEX vs OPEX modeling
- Downtime reduction and MTBF uplift as financial drivers
- Handling non-IID data and drift in multi-site deployments

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateROI(capex, opexPerMonth, savingsPerMonth, horizonMonths) {
  const totalOpex = opexPerMonth * horizonMonths;
  const totalCost = capex + totalOpex;
  const totalSavings = savingsPerMonth * horizonMonths;
  const roi = (totalSavings - totalCost) / totalCost;
  return { totalCost, totalSavings, roi };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor and mitigate model drift across sites?
- What metrics would you track to validate the ROI assumptions and trigger governance gates?

