## Why This Is Asked

Assesses designing a privacy-conscious, on-device NLP feature with energy, storage, and regulatory constraints, plus a quantified cost-benefit trade-off.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML and multilingual support
- Energy budgeting, latency targets, local storage planning
- Privacy budgets, regulatory/compliance costs, opt-in controls
- Staged rollout and metrics for go/no-go decisions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo inference loop for on-device summarization
function summarize(conversation, model) {
  // assume preloaded model in memory
  const chunk = chunkify(conversation, 512);
  return chunk.map(c => model.infer(c)).join(" ");
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate privacy guarantees during updates?
- How would you measure missed insights vs. privacy budget over time?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about client-side privacy, offline UX, and cost trade-offs without server trust. The candidate must specify concrete numbers, crypto choices, and go/no-go criteria, balancing performance, storage, and regulatory costs.

## Key Concepts

- Client-side encryption and key management
- Data growth and local cache sizing
- Delta synchronization vs full sync
- Privacy/compliance implications and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example using Web Crypto API AES-GCM
async function encrypt(plaintext, cryptoKey) {
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const encrypted = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(
    { name: 'AES-GCM', iv },
    cryptoKey,
    new TextEncoder().encode(plaintext)
  );
  return { encrypted, iv };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to translate on-device ML constraints into practical business decisions, requiring technical expertise balanced with financial analysis and strategic planning.

## Key Concepts
- On-device ML optimization and resource constraints
- Patch-based model update mechanisms
- Performance budgets (latency, energy, memory)
- Data minimization and privacy compliance
- Phased deployment and risk management

## Code Example
```javascript
// CBA calculation framework for on-device voice assistant
function calculateCBA(months, implementationCost, operationalCost, userValue, complianceCost) {
  const totalCost = implementationCost + (operationalCost * months) + (complianceCost * months);
  const totalRevenue = userValue * months;
  return {
    netValue: totalRevenue - totalCost,
    breakEvenMonth: Math.ceil(implementationCost / (userValue - operationalCost - complianceCost)),
    roi: ((totalRevenue - totalCost) / totalCost) * 100
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you estimate energy impact per utterance across different device classes?
- What metrics would you use to determine rollback triggers during regional rollout?
- How do you balance model accuracy against size constraints for on-device deployment?
- What compliance frameworks should be considered for voice data processing?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to model costs for on-device features with privacy constraints, focusing on storage, compute, telemetry, and go/no-go criteria. It emphasizes practical trade-offs and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts
- On-device compute budgeting
- Data minimization and privacy compliance
- Telemetry design and cost optimization
- Index sizing and update cadence
- Break-even analysis and milestone-driven go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeCBA(params) {
  const storageCost = params.indexMB * 0.15;
  const energyCost = params.annualWh * 0.0003;
  const telemetryCost = params.dailyTelemetryKB * 365 * 0.00001;
  const privacyAuditCost = params.userCount * 0.10;

  return {
    storageCost,
    energyCost,
    telemetryCost,
    privacyAuditCost,
    totalYear1Cost: storageCost + energyCost + telemetryCost + privacyAuditCost
  };
}
```
